==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/913004?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba","html_url":"https://github.com/mkouba","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-11-27T10:00:11Z","updated_at":"2020-11-27T10:00:11Z","body":"I can confirm that we have a bug in a loop section validation. We need to rework the validation algorithm. \r\n\r\nFor now there are 2 workarounds:\r\n1. Remove the `{@java.util.List<org.acme.qute.Item> items}` param declaration, i.e. skip the validation completely\r\n2. Redeclare the param declaration inside the loop, i.e.:\r\n```\r\n{#each item.tags('foo')}\r\n     {@java.lang.String it} <1>\r\n     {it}\r\n{/each}\r\n```\r\n<1> This tells qute to treat `it` as `String`.\r\n\r\nAnd yes, neither of the two is _acceptable_ but that's all we have :-(.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/734751854/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"mkouba","id":913004,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMzAwNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/913004?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba","html_url":"https://github.com/